<main class="br">
<section class="w hero"><div><div class="e">Brake & safety</div><h1 class="t">Brake service & repair near you</h1><p class="c">Your brakes are one of your vehicle’s most important safety systems. Our technicians inspect pads, rotors, fluid, and related components so you understand the condition of your brakes and the service they need.</p><a class="btn" href="#brake-book">Request an appointment →</a></div><img src="{{ 'ats-inline-65.jpg' | asset_url }}" alt="Technician performing a brake inspection"></section>
<section class="s a"><div class="w g2"><article class="p"><div class="e">Signs to watch for</div><h3>Signs it may be time for brake service</h3><p>Brake concerns should be checked promptly so you can drive with confidence.</p><ul class="list"><li>Squealing or grinding noises</li><li>Brake pedal feels soft or spongy</li><li>Vehicle pulls while braking</li><li>Brake warning light is on</li></ul></article><article class="p"><div class="e">What’s included</div><h3>What’s included in brake service?</h3><p>We inspect the components that help your vehicle stop safely and smoothly.</p><ul class="list"><li>Brake-pad and rotor inspection</li><li>Brake-fluid condition check</li><li>Caliper and hardware inspection</li><li>Clear recommendations before work begins</li></ul></article></div></section>
<section class="s d"><div class="w center"><div class="e">Good to know</div><h2 class="t">Brake service — how often, how long, and what it costs</h2><p class="c">Brake wear depends on driving habits, vehicle type, and road conditions. A professional inspection identifies what your vehicle needs and when.</p><div class="g3" style="margin-top:27px"><article class="p"><h3>Any brake concern</h3><p>Noise, vibration, pulling, or a warning light are all good reasons to have your brakes checked.</p></article><article class="p"><h3>Routine inspection</h3><p>Regular inspections help identify wear before it turns into a larger repair.</p></article><article class="p"><h3>Clear estimates</h3><p>Your advisor reviews service recommendations and pricing before work begins.</p></article></div></div></section>
<section class="s"><div class="w center"><div class="e">How booking works</div><h2 class="t">From request to back on the road</h2><div class="g4" style="margin-top:27px"><article class="p step"><b>1</b><h3>Request online</h3><p>Choose a nearby store.</p></article><article class="p step"><b>2</b><h3>Check in</h3><p>Tell us what you have noticed.</p></article><article class="p step"><b>3</b><h3>Inspect & quote</h3><p>We check your brake system and explain the findings.</p></article><article class="p step"><b>4</b><h3>Back on the road</h3><p>Leave with a clear service summary.</p></article></div></div></section>
<section class="s a"><div class="w split"><img src="{{ 'ats-inline-65.jpg' | asset_url }}" alt="Brake service at American Tire Stores"><div><div class="e">Why it matters</div><h2 class="t">Why brake service matters</h2><p class="c">Reliable brakes support safe stopping, stable handling, and everyday confidence. Addressing wear early can help protect other brake components from additional damage.</p><ul class="list"><li>Supports safe and consistent stopping</li><li>Helps prevent rotor and caliper damage</li><li>Identifies fluid or hydraulic concerns</li><li>Gives you a clear picture of brake condition</li></ul></div></div></section>
<section class="s"><div class="w center"><div class="e">Brake components</div><h2 class="t">Pads, rotors, and what wears out</h2><p class="c">Different parts wear at different rates. An inspection helps identify exactly what your vehicle needs.</p><div class="g3" style="margin-top:27px"><article class="p"><h3>Brake pads</h3><p>Friction material wears over time and should be replaced before it is too thin.</p></article><article class="p"><h3>Rotors</h3><p>Rotors are measured for wear and condition as part of the brake inspection.</p></article><article class="p"><h3>Brake fluid</h3><p>Fluid condition matters for responsive braking and the health of hydraulic components.</p></article></div></div></section>
<section class="s d"><div class="w center"><div class="e">Quality you can trust</div><h2 class="t">Quality parts, every time</h2><p class="c">We recommend brake service based on your vehicle’s condition and use quality components suited to the job.</p><div class="g3" style="margin-top:27px"><article class="p"><h3>Professional inspection</h3><p>We identify the condition of pads, rotors, hardware, and fluid before recommending repairs.</p></article><article class="p"><h3>Vehicle-matched service</h3><p>Parts and procedures are selected for your vehicle’s requirements.</p></article><article class="p"><h3>Clear communication</h3><p>You will understand the findings and next steps before authorizing work.</p></article></div></div></section>
<section class="s a"><div class="w split"><img src="{{ 'ats-inline-67.jpg' | asset_url }}" alt="Customer discussing brake service"><div><div class="e">Straightforward options</div><h2 class="t">What does brake service cost?</h2><p class="c">Pricing depends on your vehicle, brake condition, and the components needed. Select a location to request service and your advisor can confirm the right recommendation. Financing is available for qualifying customers.</p><a class="btn" href="/pages/financing">Explore financing →</a></div></div></section>
<section class="s d" id="brake-book"><div class="w center"><div class="e">Request an appointment</div><h2 class="t">Book brake service at your store</h2><p class="c">Choose your nearest American Tire Stores location to begin your brake-service request.</p><div class="book"><div class="row"><select id="brake-store" aria-label="Choose a store"><option value="">Choose your store</option><option value="52820">Ventura</option><option value="52819">Thousand Oaks</option><option value="52819">Valencia</option><option value="61758">Hollywood</option><option value="52816">Glendale</option><option value="52818">Glendale 2</option><option value="52814">Bellflower</option><option value="52814">Costa Mesa</option><option value="52815">Cathedral City</option></select><button type="button" class="btn" onclick="window.startBrakeBooking()">Request brake service →</button></div><div id="brake-widget" class="widget">Choose a store above to begin your brake-service request.</div></div></div></section>
<section class="s"><div class="w center"><div class="e">Why American Tire Stores</div><h2 class="t">Service Southern California drivers trust</h2><div class="g3" style="margin-top:27px"><article class="p"><div class="stars">★★★★★</div><p>“They identified the brake noise, explained the work clearly, and had me driving confidently again.”</p><b>American Tire Stores customer</b></article><article class="p"><div class="stars">★★★★★</div><p>“Professional inspection and no pressure. I knew exactly what was needed before the work started.”</p><b>American Tire Stores customer</b></article><article class="p"><div class="stars">★★★★★</div><p>“Quick booking, excellent communication, and smooth brakes when I left.”</p><b>American Tire Stores customer</b></article></div></div></section>
<section class="s a"><div class="w center"><div class="e">Near you</div><h2 class="t">Brake service near you, across Southern California</h2><p class="c">Brake inspections and repairs are available at all nine American Tire Stores locations.</p><div class="locs"><article class="loc"><h3>Ventura</h3><p>5100 Telegraph Rd<br>(805) 644-3330</p><a href="/pages/location-ventura-ca">Store details →</a></article><article class="loc"><h3>Thousand Oaks</h3><p>621 E Thousand Oaks Blvd<br>(805) 379-1910</p><a href="/pages/location-thousand-oaks-ca">Store details →</a></article><article class="loc"><h3>Valencia</h3><p>23510 Valencia Blvd, Unit A<br>(661) 596-1444</p><a href="/pages/location-valencia-ca">Store details →</a></article><article class="loc"><h3>Hollywood</h3><p>1174 N Western Ave<br>(323) 372-9372</p><a href="/pages/location-hollywood-ca">Store details →</a></article><article class="loc"><h3>Glendale</h3><p>737 S Glendale Ave<br>(818) 243-3191</p><a href="/pages/location-glendale-ca">Store details →</a></article><article class="loc"><h3>Glendale 2</h3><p>1130 S Central Ave<br>(818) 547-2010</p><a href="/pages/location-glendale-ii-ca">Store details →</a></article><article class="loc"><h3>Bellflower</h3><p>9509 Alondra Blvd<br>(562) 804-4737</p><a href="/pages/location-bellflower-ca">Store details →</a></article><article class="loc"><h3>Costa Mesa</h3><p>2049 Harbor Blvd<br>(949) 802-6419</p><a href="/pages/location-costa-mesa-ca">Store details →</a></article><article class="loc"><h3>Cathedral City</h3><p>68406 E Palm Canyon Dr<br>(760) 469-9510</p><a href="/pages/location-cathedral-city-ca">Store details →</a></article></div></div></section>
<section class="s"><div class="w center"><div class="e">More services</div><h2 class="t">Related auto services</h2><div class="g3 rel" style="margin-top:27px"><article class="p"><img src="{{ 'ats-inline-64.jpg' | asset_url }}" alt="Wheel alignment"><div class="body"><h3>Wheel alignment</h3><p>Support even tire wear and stable steering.</p><a href="/pages/service-wheel-alignment">Learn more →</a></div></article><article class="p"><img src="{{ 'ats-inline-66.jpg' | asset_url }}" alt="Tire installation"><div class="body"><h3>Tire installation</h3><p>Professional installation for tires that fit your vehicle.</p><a href="/pages/service-tire-installation">Learn more →</a></div></article><article class="p"><img src="{{ 'ats-inline-68.jpg' | asset_url }}" alt="TPMS service"><div class="body"><h3>TPMS service</h3><p>Diagnose tire-pressure monitoring concerns.</p><a href="/pages/service-tpms">Learn more →</a></div></article></div></div></section>
<section class="s a"><div class="w center"><div class="e">Good to know</div><h2 class="t">Brake service FAQ</h2><div class="faq"><details><summary>How do I know if I need brake service?</summary><p>Squealing, grinding, a soft brake pedal, pulling during braking, vibration, or a warning light are reasons to arrange an inspection.</p></details><details><summary>How often should brakes be inspected?</summary><p>Brake inspection is a good idea during routine tire service, when you notice a change, or according to your vehicle’s maintenance schedule.</p></details><details><summary>Can you replace pads and rotors?</summary><p>Yes. We inspect pad and rotor condition and recommend the service appropriate for your vehicle.</p></details><details><summary>How long does brake service take?</summary><p>Timing depends on the work required. Your selected store can confirm the expected time during booking.</p></details><details><summary>Is an appointment required?</summary><p>An appointment is recommended so the store can reserve time and confirm availability.</p></details></div></div></section>
<section class="final"><div class="w"><div class="e">Drive with confidence</div><h2 class="t">Ready for brake service?</h2><p class="c">Request an appointment at your nearest American Tire Stores location today.</p><a class="btn" href="#brake-book">Request an appointment →</a></div></section>
</main>
